  "output": "## Performance Analysis\n\nThis is an early-stage Next.js 16 App Router codebase (Server Components + Drizzle/Postgres + Clerk). Only the `sources` feature is implemented so far — `runs`, `conflicts`, `rules`, `audit` don't exist as pages yet. That significantly limits what's actually present to fix. Here's what I found, calibrated to what's real versus hypothetical.\n\n### 1. N+1 query patterns\n**None currently** — there's exactly one query path (`listSources`), a flat `select().from(sources)`. No loops issuing per-row queries exist yet. Worth revisiting once `runs`/`entities`/`matches` pages are built, since `entities` has a `runId, sourceId, externalId` composite index (`lib/db/schema.ts:115`) that suggests per-row entity lookups are coming — watch for that pattern then.\n\n### 2. Unnecessary React re-renders\n**None found** — zero `useState`/`useEffect`/`useMemo`/`useCallback` in the codebase. Everything is a Server Component except small, static `\"use client\"` leaves (`nav-rail.tsx`, motion wrappers, sign-out control). `NavRail` re-renders on every route change via `usePathname()`, but that's expected/necessary for the active-link indicator and is cheap (a handful of `<li>`s).\n\n### 3. Caching opportunities — this is the real finding\n\n`lib/server/sources.ts:23-30`:\n\n```ts\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const all = await listSources();   // full table scan + zod re-parse\n  return { crm: ..., warehouse: ..., synthetic: ... };\n}\n```\n\nTwo problems:\n- **No request-level memoization.** Drizzle calls aren't deduped by Next the way `fetch()` is. If any future page ever calls both `listSources()` and `countSourcesBySide()` in the same render (e.g., a sources page that also shows a summary strip), that's 2 DB round trips + 2 full zod-parse passes for identical data.\n- Every `countSourcesBySide()` call re-fetches and re-validates the whole table just to count.\n\nFix — wrap in React's `cache()` for request-scoped dedup, and derive the count from the same fetch instead of an independent one:\n\n```ts\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\n\nexport const listSources = cache(async (): Promise<Source[]> => {\n  await connection();\n  const rows = await getDb().select().from(sources).orderBy(sources.createdAt);\n  return rows.map((row) => sourceSchema.parse(row));\n});\n\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const all = await listSources(); // now dedupes against any other call in the same request\n  return {\n    crm: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"salesforce\" || s.kind === \"hubspot\").length,\n    warehouse: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"databricks\" || s.kind === \"snowflake\").length,\n    synthetic: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"synthetic\").length,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nFor cross-request caching (sources change rarely — only via explicit \"Add source\" actions), `unstable_cache` with a tag is a good fit, invalidated on writes:\n\n```ts\nimport { unstable_cache, revalidateTag } from \"next/cache\";\n\nexport const listSources = unstable_cache(\n  async () => {\n    await connection();\n    const rows = await getDb().select().from(sources).orderBy(sources.createdAt);\n    return rows.map((row) => sourceSchema.parse(row));\n  },\n  [\"sources-list\"],\n  { tags: [\"sources\"] },\n);\n\n// call revalidateTag(\"sources\") wherever a source is created/edited\n```\n\n### 4. Memory leaks\n**None found.** No intervals, subscriptions, event listeners, or unclosed effects anywhere in the code — there's nothing yet that could leak. `getDb()` (`lib/db/index.ts:27`) correctly caches the Postgres connection on `globalThis` to survive HMR reloads rather than opening a new pool each time, which is the right pattern here.\n\n### 5. Redundant computations\n- `countSourcesBySide` re-derives from a fresh fetch instead of reusing an existing `Source[]` the caller may already have — covered above.\n- `SOURCE_KIND_LABEL[source.kind]` / `SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[source.kind]` lookups in `source-table.tsx` are already O(1) map lookups per row — fine, no action needed.\n- `useReducedMotion()` is called independently in 4 separate client components (`landing-hero`, `pipeline-strip`, `get-started-hero`, `step-list`). Each mounts its own `matchMedia` listener. Not a leak (Motion cleans it up), but if more animated components get added, consider a single `MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"` provider at the layout root instead of per-component hooks — one listener instead of N.\n\n### Bottom line\nThe codebase is too early-stage for most of the categories you asked about to have real instances yet. The one concrete, worth-fixing issue is `countSourcesBySide`'s redundant fetch/parse in `lib/server/sources.ts` — wrap `listSources` in `cache()` (and optionally `unstable_cache`) before the `runs`/`conflicts` pages get built, since those will multiply this pattern.\n",
